new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8521e1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: added a `markdown` format to `render()`. It uses the vendored `tabulate` with `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`, followed by a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown`.
+- `README.md`: documented the option.
+- No tests, `vendor/` files or dependencies were changed.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -W error -m unittest`: 3 tests ran, all OK. That includes the existing `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`. `-W error` was used so a tabulate DeprecationWarning would fail the run.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown`: printed the expected table and total.
+
+## Not verified / caveats
+- I did not test cells containing `|` characters. The vendored `pipe` style does not escape them, so such a SKU or name would break the table. Fixing that would need a platform-team change to `vendor/tabulate` or escaping in `report.py`.
+- I added no new tests, because the existing ones already cover the exact output.
